---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility - Accessible UI Kit">
  <main id="main-content" class="docs-page">
    <article class="docs-content">
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p class="lead">Our commitment to making the web usable for everyone.</p>

      <section id="standards" aria-labelledby="standards-heading">
        <h2 id="standards-heading">Standards We Follow</h2>
        <p>All components are designed to meet or exceed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> — Web Content Accessibility Guidelines</li>
          <li>
            <strong>RGAA 4.1</strong> — Référentiel Général d'Amélioration de l'Accessibilité (French
            standard)
          </li>
          <li><strong>WAI-ARIA 1.2</strong> — When native HTML isn't sufficient</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
        <h2 id="principles-heading">Our Principles</h2>

        <h3>1. Semantic HTML First</h3>
        <p>
          We use the right HTML elements for the job. A button is a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>, not
          a styled <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>. This gives us keyboard support, focus management, and
          screen reader announcements for free.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Keyboard Navigation</h3>
        <p>Every interactive component works with keyboard only:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><kbd>Tab</kbd> moves between focusable elements</li>
          <li><kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Space</kbd> activate buttons and links</li>
          <li><kbd>Arrow keys</kbd> navigate within composite widgets</li>
          <li><kbd>Escape</kbd> closes modals and dropdowns</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. Visible Focus</h3>
        <p>
          Focus indicators are never hidden. Our default focus ring is a 2px solid outline with 2px
          offset, using the primary brand color for visibility.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Color Is Not Enough</h3>
        <p>
          We never rely on color alone to convey information. Error states use icons, text, and
          color together. Links are underlined by default.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Respect User Preferences</h3>
        <p>Components respect system preferences:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> — Disables animations</li>
          <li><code>prefers-color-scheme</code> — Supports light/dark themes</li>
          <li>Browser font size settings — All sizes use relative units</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>6. ARIA: Use Sparingly</h3>
        <p>
          The first rule of ARIA is "don't use ARIA" if native HTML works. We only add ARIA
          attributes when necessary, and we ensure they're correct.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="testing" aria-labelledby="testing-heading">
        <h2 id="testing-heading">How We Test</h2>

        <h3>Automated Testing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>axe-core</strong> — Catches common violations</li>
          <li><strong>Playwright</strong> — Keyboard navigation testing</li>
          <li><strong>Lighthouse</strong> — Accessibility audits in CI</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Manual Testing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Keyboard-only navigation</li>
          <li>Screen reader testing (NVDA, VoiceOver)</li>
          <li>High contrast mode</li>
          <li>200% zoom</li>
          <li>Reduced motion</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="checklist" aria-labelledby="checklist-heading">
        <h2 id="checklist-heading">Component Checklist</h2>
        <p>Every component must pass this checklist before release:</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Uses semantic HTML elements</li>
          <li>Works with keyboard only</li>
          <li>Has visible focus indicator</li>
          <li>Meets color contrast requirements (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI)</li>
          <li>Works at 200% zoom</li>
          <li>Has accessible name (visible or via aria-label)</li>
          <li>Announces state changes to screen readers</li>
          <li>Respects prefers-reduced-motion</li>
          <li>Passes axe-core automated tests</li>
          <li>Tested with at least one screen reader</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-heading">
        <h2 id="resources-heading">Resources</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >WCAG 2.1 Quick Reference</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://accessibilite.numerique.gouv.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >RGAA (French)</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >ARIA Authoring Practices Guide</a
            >
          </li>
          <li><a href="https://webaim.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WebAIM</a></li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://a11yproject.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The A11Y Project</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .docs-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .docs-content h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .docs-content section:first-of-type h2 {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .docs-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .docs-content p {
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .docs-content ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .docs-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  kbd {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.125em 0.5em;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .checklist li {
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    position: relative;
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: '☐';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }
</style>
